I think I've been playing NetHack since about 1987 or so and I have yet
to ascend, or even start a quest.  I have gotten to see the quest level
with an A, an M, and a W, all within the past couple of months.

My problem seems to be a tendency to take risks that the game has
definitely not rewarded.  I also find, though, that even if am being
super-careful (and even occasionally using the E-word), I find myself
mobbed by nasties and caught in absolutely ridiculous situations.
Fundamentally NetHack just isn't fair -- there are plenty of times I get
into situations that no amount of patience or cleverness could get me
out of, and sometimes I am quite sure through no fault of my own.
Getting a character to the point of being relatively safe against the
dangers of the dungeon is really more a matter of luck than skill, but
one is always tempted to think that some kind of cleverness would have
saved the day even when it really wouldn't have.

Seeing all these ascension stories is just damned annoying.  So is
having people say "oh, all you need is reflection and magic-resistance
and foo-resistance and bar-resistance and a big stack of blessed scrolls
of charging and etc." when, of course, getting the complete collection
of survival tools is so damned hard in the first place.

On average, I've been getting better at and farther into the game
lately, and really deeply realizing that I need to treat NetHack more
like a game of chess than a game of Quake is one of the reasons.  I also
gave up and read spoilers -- and discovered there were things I _never_
would have thought of trying or been able to discover through
experimentation.

